# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependencies
# Reinstalled from package-lock.json on every machine and every deploy.
# node_modules/ has no leading slash on purpose: it matches at any depth, so
# this covers the root workspace and client/ and server/ in one line.
# The lock files themselves ARE committed -- that is the point of a lock file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output
# Regenerated by `npm --prefix client run build` and `npm --prefix server run build`.
# No leading slash, so it covers client/dist/ and server/dist/ alike.
# Vercel builds the client itself on its own infrastructure, so there is never
# a reason to upload a compiled bundle.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
dist/
build/
out/
.vite/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets -- the important one
# A .env holding a Vercel token or a Colyseus key must never reach a remote.
# Negation last, so .env.example stays committable as a template while every
# real environment file is ignored.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs and crash dumps
# Our own dev logs and whatever a package manager leaves behind on a failure.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
logs/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*
report.[0-9]*.[0-9]*.[0-9]*.[0-9]*.json
pids/
*.pid
*.seed
*.pid.lock

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Caches
# tsconfig.tsbuildinfo makes `tsc --noEmit` incremental; it embeds absolute
# paths from whichever machine wrote it, so it is useless everywhere else.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.tsbuildinfo
.cache/
.eslintcache
.stylelintcache
.parcel-cache/
.turbo/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test and coverage output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
coverage/
.nyc_output/
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
.playwright/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor and OS cruft
# Personal keybindings and project files should not become part of the repo,
# but .vscode/extensions.json is deliberately NOT listed above so shared
# recommended extensions can still be committed by hand.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
ehthumbs.db
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deploy tooling
# .vercel/ holds the link back to a personal project. Committing it points
# someone else's clone at your account.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vercel/
.netlify/
.wrangler/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local scratch
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
tmp/
temp/
scratch/
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
client/test-audio.stub.mjs
